    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Question\n\nIs there a way to disable this feature? https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.surround/commit/fc6fbc319b2d686c524d71c7feda20f71af15b8e \r\n\r\nI liked how it worked previously, where if there is a long delay between \"s\" and another key - it actually sends the built-in \"s\" key.\r\n\r\nWhen I use surround, I press \"s\" followed by the respective key within the timeout len to activate the surround feature.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.surround</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a way to disable this feature? <a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.surround/commit/fc6fbc319b2d686c524d71c7feda20f71af15b8e/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.surround/commit/fc6fbc319b2d686c524d71c7feda20f71af15b8e\">nvim-mini/mini.surround@<tt>fc6fbc3</tt></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I liked how it worked previously, where if there is a long delay between \"s\" and another key - it actually sends the built-in \"s\" key.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When I use surround, I press \"s\" followed by the respective key within the timeout len to activate the surround feature.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.surround\nQuestion\nIs there a way to disable this feature? nvim-mini/mini.surround@fc6fbc3\nI liked how it worked previously, where if there is a long delay between \"s\" and another key - it actually sends the built-in \"s\" key.\nWhen I use surround, I press \"s\" followed by the respective key within the timeout len to activate the surround feature.",
