            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, you can add `vim.keymap.del({ 'n', 'x' }, 's')` *after* `require('mini.surround').setup()` call. If you don't use `sa` for `add` action, use only `vim.keymap.del('n', 's')`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, you can add <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.keymap.del({ 'n', 'x' }, 's')</code> <em>after</em> <code class=\"notranslate\">require('mini.surround').setup()</code> call. If you don't use <code class=\"notranslate\">sa</code> for <code class=\"notranslate\">add</code> action, use only <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.keymap.del('n', 's')</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Yes, you can add vim.keymap.del({ 'n', 'x' }, 's') after require('mini.surround').setup() call. If you don't use sa for add action, use only vim.keymap.del('n', 's').",
